I'll analyze the requirements and implement the `solve()` method for the `WordProblemSolver` class.

The solution needs to:
1. Parse math word problems in the format "What is X plus/minus/multiplied by/divided by Y?"
2. Evaluate left-to-right, ignoring standard order of operations
3. Reject unsupported operations, non-math questions, and invalid syntax

WordProblemSolver.java
```java
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

class WordProblemSolver {
    private static final Map<String, Integer> OPERATIONS = new HashMap<>();

    static {
        OPERATIONS.put("plus", 1);
        OPERATIONS.put("minus", 2);
        OPERATIONS.put("multiplied", 3);
        OPERATIONS.put("divided", 4);
    }

    int solve(final String wordProblem) {
        if (!wordProblem.startsWith("What is") || !wordProblem.endsWith("?")) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid problem format");
        }

        String problem = wordProblem
                .substring("What is".length(), wordProblem.length() - 1)
                .trim();

        if (problem.endsWith("?")) {
            problem = problem.substring(0, problem.length() - 1).trim();
        }

        String[] tokens = problem.split(" ");

        if (tokens.length == 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid problem format");
        }

        int result = parseNumber(tokens[0]);
        int index = 1;

        while (index < tokens.length) {
            String operation = tokens[index];
            int operationCode = OPERATIONS.get(operation);

            if (operationCode == -1) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Unsupported operation");
            }

            if (index + 1 >= tokens.length) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid syntax");
            }

            int nextNumber = parseNumber(tokens[index + 1]);

            switch (operationCode) {
                case 1:
                    result = result + nextNumber;
                    break;
                case 2:
                    result = result - nextNumber;
                    break;
                case 3:
                    result = result * nextNumber;
                    break;
                case 4:
                    result = result / nextNumber;
                    break;
            }

            index += 2;
        }

        return result;
    }

    private int parseNumber(String token) {
        try {
            return Integer.parseInt(token);
        } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid syntax");
        }
    }
}
