I'll implement the School roster system. The implementation needs to:
1. Store students by grade
2. Prevent adding the same student to multiple grades
3. Return sorted grades
4. Return sorted students within a grade
5. Return all students sorted by grade and then alphabetically

I'll use a `HashMap<u32, Vec<String>>` to store students by grade, with methods to add, get grades, and get specific grades.

lib.rs
```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;

pub struct School {
    roster: HashMap<u32, Vec<String>>,
}

impl School {
    pub fn new() -> School {
        School {
            roster: HashMap::new(),
        }
    }

    pub fn add(&mut self, grade: u32, student: &str) {
        // Check if the student is already in the roster (any grade)
        for students in self.roster.values() {
            if students.iter().any(|s| s == student) {
                return;
            }
        }
        
        let entry = self.roster.entry(grade).or_insert_with(Vec::new);
        entry.push(student.to_string());
    }

    pub fn grades(&self) -> Vec<u32> {
        let mut grades: Vec<u32> = self.roster.keys().cloned().collect();
        grades.sort();
        grades
    }

    pub fn grade(&self, grade: u32) -> Vec<String> {
        let mut students = self.roster.get(&grade).cloned().unwrap_or_default();
        students.sort();
        students
    }
}
```
