The issue is that `is_allergic_to` relies on `std::distance` between the set's 
`begin()` and the found iterator matching the index of the value in the `values`
array. But `unordered_set` has no defined iteration order, so the index from 
`std::distance` won't reliably correspond to the correct power-of-2 value.



I'll use a vector of pairs to guarantee consistent ordering and correct value 
mapping.



