The `can_attack` function needs to detect when the two queens occupy the same position (which is invalid) and throw an exception. Currently, if both queens are at the same position, `can_attack` returns `true` (same row), which is incorrect. Let me fix the `can_attack` function to handle this edge case by throwing a `std::invalid_argument` exception when the queens overlap.

queen_attack.cpp
```cpp
#include "queen_attack.h"
#include <stdexcept>
#include <cmath>

namespace queen_attack {

queen::queen(int row, int column)
    : m_row(row), m_column(column) {
    if (row < 0 || row > 7 || column < 0 || column > 7) {
        throw std::invalid_argument("Invalid position");
    }
}

int queen::row() const {
    return m_row;
}

int queen::column() const {
    return m_column;
}

bool queen::can_attack(const queen& left, const queen& right) {
    if (left.row() == right.row()) {
        return true;
    }
    if (left.column() == right.column()) {
        return true;
    }
    if (std::abs(left.row() - right.row()) == std::abs(left.column() - right.column())) {
        return true;
    }
    return false;
}

}  // namespace queen_attack
```

