Looking at the linker errors, the issue is that the template methods are defined
in `linked_list.cpp` but templates must be fully visible at the point of 
instantiation. Since `linked_list.cpp` doesn't `#include "linked_list.h"`, the 
compiler can't see the class definition when it processes the template method 
definitions, causing the linker to not find the symbols.



The fix is to add the `#include "linked_list.h"` at the top of 
`linked_list.cpp`.



