The root cause of the linker errors was that `linked_list.cpp` defined template 
methods for `List<T>` but never included the header that declares the `List` 
class. Without the header, the compiler couldn't associate the `List<T>::method`
definitions with the class, so the symbols were never properly emitted for the 
linker to resolve. Adding `#include "linked_list.h"` fixes this.

