The error is that `newBase` is being referenced in the constructor, but it's only available as a parameter to `convertToBase`. The conversion logic should move to `convertToBase`.

BaseConverter.java
```java
class BaseConverter {
    private final int originalBase;
    private final int[] originalDigits;

    BaseConverter(int originalBase, int[] originalDigits) {
        if (originalBase < 2) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid base value.");
        }
        for (int digit : originalDigits) {
            if (digit < 0) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid value for digit.");
            }
            if (digit >= originalBase) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid value for digit.");
            }
        }
        this.originalBase = originalBase;
        this.originalDigits = originalDigits;
    }

    int[] convertToBase(int newBase) {
        if (newBase < 2) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid base value.");
        }

        // Convert to decimal first
        long decimalValue = 0;
        for (int digit : originalDigits) {
            decimalValue = decimalValue * originalBase + digit;
        }

        // Handle zero specially
        if (decimalValue == 0) {
            return new int[]{0};
        }

        // Convert decimal to new base
        java.util.List<Integer> digits = new java.util.ArrayList<>();
        while (decimalValue > 0) {
            digits.add(0, (int)(decimalValue % newBase));
            decimalValue /= newBase;
        }

        int[] result = new int[digits.size()];
        for (int i = 0; i < digits.size(); i++) {
            result[i] = digits.get(i);
        }
        return result;
    }
}
```
