Looking at the test failures, I need to update the error messages to match what the tests expect, and fix the order of validation checks (punctuation check before length check, and handle the case where punctuation results in wrong digit count).

The tests expect these messages:
- "must not be fewer than 10 digits" (not "incorrect number of digits")
- "must not be greater than 11 digits" (not "more than 11 digits")
- "area code cannot start with zero" (not "0")
- "area code cannot start with one" (not "1")
- "exchange code cannot start with zero"
- "exchange code cannot start with one"
- "punctuations not permitted"

PhoneNumber.java
```
class PhoneNumber {

    private final String number;

    PhoneNumber(String numberString) {
        if (numberString.chars().anyMatch(Character::isLetter)) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("letters not permitted");
        }

        if (numberString.chars().anyMatch(c -> {
            char ch = (char) c;
            return "!@:-+.".indexOf(ch) != -1;
        })) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("punctuations not permitted");
        }

        String digitsOnly = numberString.replaceAll("\\D", "");

        if (digitsOnly.length() < 10) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("must not be fewer than 10 digits");
        }

        if (digitsOnly.length() > 11) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("must not be greater than 11 digits");
        }

        if (digitsOnly.length() == 11) {
            if (digitsOnly.charAt(0) != '1') {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("11 digits must start with 1");
            }
            digitsOnly = digitsOnly.substring(1);
        }

        if (digitsOnly.length() != 10) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("incorrect number of digits");
        }

        char areaCodeFirstDigit = digitsOnly.charAt(0);
        char exchangeCodeFirstDigit = digitsOnly.charAt(3);

        if (areaCodeFirstDigit == '0') {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("area code cannot start with zero");
        }

        if (areaCodeFirstDigit == '1') {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("area code cannot start with one");
        }

        if (exchangeCodeFirstDigit == '0') {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("exchange code cannot start with zero");
        }

        if (exchangeCodeFirstDigit == '1') {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("exchange code cannot start with one");
        }

        this.number = digitsOnly;
    }

    String getNumber() {
        return number;
    }
}
```
