I'll implement a `CustomSet` class using a `HashMap` as the underlying data structure. Since all methods operate on the generic type `T`, I'll use a `HashMap<T, Object>` where the value is a constant placeholder.

Let me implement all the methods:

- `isEmpty()`: check if the map is empty
- `contains(element)`: check if the map contains the key
- `isDisjoint(other)`: check if there's no intersection
- `add(element)`: add to the map, return whether it was newly added
- `equals(obj)`: check set equality by comparing contents
- `getIntersection(other)`: elements in both sets
- `getUnion(other)`: all elements from both sets
- `getDifference(other)`: elements in this set but not in other
- `isSubset(other)`: all elements of this set are in other

Here's the implementation:

CustomSet.java
```java
import java.util.Collection;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

class CustomSet<T> {
    private Map<T, Object> data;
    private static final Object PRESENT = new Object();

    CustomSet() {
        data = new HashMap<T, Object>();
    }

    CustomSet(Collection<T> data) {
        this.data = new HashMap<T, Object>();
        for (T element : data) {
            this.data.put(element, PRESENT);
        }
    }

    boolean isEmpty() {
        return data.isEmpty();
    }

    boolean contains(T element) {
        return data.containsKey(element);
    }

    boolean isDisjoint(CustomSet<T> other) {
        for (T element : data.keySet()) {
            if (other.data.containsKey(element)) {
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }

    boolean add(T element) {
        if (data.containsKey(element)) {
            return false;
        }
        data.put(element, PRESENT);
        return true;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object obj) {
        if (this == obj) {
            return true;
        }
        if (!(obj instanceof CustomSet)) {
            return false;
        }
        CustomSet<T> other = (CustomSet<T>) obj;
        if (data.size() != other.data.size()) {
            return false;
        }
        if (data.equals(other.data)) {
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    }

    CustomSet<T> getIntersection(CustomSet<T> other) {
        CustomSet<T> result = new CustomSet<T>();
        for (T element : data.keySet()) {
            if (other.data.containsKey(element)) {
                result.data.put(element, PRESENT);
            }
        }
        return result;
    }

    CustomSet<T> getUnion(CustomSet<T> other) {
        CustomSet<T> result = new CustomSet<T>();
        for (T element : data.keySet()) {
            result.data.put(element, PRESENT);
        }
        for (T element : other.data.keySet()) {
            result.data.put(element, PRESENT);
        }
        return result;
    }

    CustomSet<T> getDifference(CustomSet<T> other) {
        CustomSet<T> result = new CustomSet<T>();
        for (T element : data.keySet()) {
            if (!other.data.containsKey(element)) {
                result.data.put(element, PRESENT);
            }
        }
        return result;
    }

    boolean isSubset(CustomSet<T> other) {
        for (T element : data.keySet()) {
            if (!other.data.containsKey(element)) {
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```
