response:
The tests timed out because the current implementation has exponential complexity—it tries all subsets at every recursion level without memoization, and the `solve` method creates a memo map but never uses it.

The key insight is that we only need to consider grouping by *set size* (1, 2, 3, 4, or 5 books), not all arbitrary subsets. This dramatically reduces the search space. We use dynamic programming with memoization on the canonical (sorted) representation of book counts.

The algorithm:
1. Count how many copies of each book we have
2. At each step, try forming a set of each possible size (1-5), taking one of each of the top-counted available books
3. Recursively calculate the cost of the remaining books
4. Return the minimum total cost

This is efficient because we only consider 5 possible groupings at each step (by size), and memoization prevents recomputation.

BookStore.java
```java
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

class BookStore {

    private static final double BOOK_PRICE = 8.0;

    private static final double[] DISCOUNTS = {
        0.0, 0.05, 0.10, 0.20, 0.25
    };

    double calculateBasketCost(List<Integer> books) {
        if (books == null || books.isEmpty()) {
            return 0.0;
        }

        // Count the number of each book
        int[] counts = new int[5];
        for (int book : books) {
            counts[book - 1]++;
        }

        Map<String, Double> memo = new HashMap<>();
        return calculateMinimumCost(counts, memo);
    }

    private double calculateMinimumCost(int[] counts, Map<String, Double> memo) {
        // Check if all counts are zero
        boolean allZero = true;
        for (int count : counts) {
            if (count > 0) {
                allZero = false;
                break;
            }
        }
        if (allZero) {
            return 0.0;
        }

        // Create a canonical form (sorted, descending) for memoization
        int[] sorted = counts.clone();
        Arrays.sort(sorted);
        // Reverse to descending
        for (int i = 0; i < sorted.length / 2; i++) {
            int temp = sorted[i];
            sorted[i] = sorted[sorted.length - 1 - i];
            sorted[sorted.length - 1 - i] = temp;
        }

        String key = Arrays.toString(sorted);
        if (memo.containsKey(key)) {
            return memo.get(key);
        }

        // Try forming a group of each possible size (1-5 books)
        double minCost = Double.MAX_VALUE;
        for (int groupSize = 1; groupSize <= 5; groupSize++) {
            // Check if we have enough distinct books for this group size
            int distinctCount = 0;
            for (int count : counts) {
                if (count > 0) {
                    distinctCount++;
                }
            }
            if (distinctCount < groupSize) {
                continue;
            }

            // Create new counts, taking one of each of the top groupSize counts
            int[] newCounts = counts.clone();
            // Sort indices by count descending
            Integer[] indices = new Integer[counts.length];
            for (int i = 0; i < indices.length; i++) {
                indices[i] = i;
            }
            Arrays.sort(indices, (a, b) -> Integer.compare(counts[b], counts[a]));
            
            // Take one book from each of the top groupSize distinct books
            boolean valid = true;
            for (int i = 0; i < groupSize; i++) {
                if (counts[indices[i]] > 0) {
                    newCounts[indices[i]]--;
                } else {
                    valid = false;
                    break;
                }
            }
            
            if (!valid) {
                continue;
            }
            
            // Calculate cost of this group
            double groupCost = groupSize * BOOK_PRICE * (1 - DISCOUNTS[groupSize - 1]);
            
            // Recursively calculate the rest
            double restCost = calculateMinimumCost(newCounts, memo);
            double total = groupCost + restCost;
            
            if (total < minCost) {
                minCost = total;
            }
        }

        memo.put(key, minCost);
        return minCost;
    }
}
```
