Looking at the test errors, the issue is that `restricted` is `undefined` when no restricted array is passed (the tests only pass the cage value in many cases). I need to handle the case where `restricted` might be undefined.

Let me analyze the test failures:
- All tests fail with `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'includes')`
- This happens because `restricted` is `undefined` in some test cases

The fix is to default `restricted` to an empty array when it's not provided.

killer-sudoku-helper.js
```
//
// This is only a SKELETON file for the 'Killer Sudoku Helper' exercise. It's been provided as a
// convenience to get you started writing code faster.
//

export const combinations = (cage, restricted = []) => {
  const results = [];
  const findCombinations = (start, target, current) => {
    if (target === 0) {
      results.push([...current]);
      return;
    }
    for (let i = start; i <= 9; i++) {
      if (restricted.includes(i)) continue;
      if (i > target) continue;
      current.push(i);
      findCombinations(i + 1, target - i, current);
      current.pop();
    }
  };

  findCombinations(1, cage, []);
  return results;
};
```
