Looking at the test failures, I can see two issues:

1. **ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException**: The `DAYS` array has an empty string at index 0, so valid indices are 0-11, but verse numbers 1-12 need indices 1-12. I need to add an extra element to make room.

2. **Missing trailing newline**: Each verse needs a trailing newline character, and the `verses` method needs to add an extra newline after each verse.

Let me fix both issues:

TwelveDays.java
```java
class TwelveDays {
    private static final String[] DAYS = {
        "", "first", "second", "third", "fourth", "fifth", "sixth",
        "seventh", "eighth", "ninth", "tenth", "eleventh", "twelfth"
    };

    private static final String[] GIFTS = {
        "", "a Partridge in a Pear Tree.",
        "two Turtle Doves",
        "three French Hens",
        "four Calling Birds",
        "five Gold Rings",
        "six Geese-a-Laying",
        "seven Swans-a-Swimming",
        "eight Maids-a-Milking",
        "nine Ladies Dancing",
        "ten Lords-a-Leaping",
        "eleven Pipers Piping",
        "twelve Drummers Drumming"
    };

    String verse(int verseNumber) {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        sb.append("On the ").append(DAYS[verseNumber]).append(" day of Christmas my true love gave to me: ");

        for (int day = verseNumber; day >= 1; day--) {
            if (day == 1 && verseNumber > 1) {
                sb.append("and ").append(GIFTS[1]);
            } else {
                sb.append(GIFTS[day]);
            }
            if (day > 1) {
                sb.append(", ");
            }
        }

        sb.append("\n");
        return sb.toString();
    }

    String verses(int startVerse, int endVerse) {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (int verse = startVerse; verse <= endVerse; verse++) {
            sb.append(verse(verse));
            sb.append("\n");
        }
        return sb.toString();
    }

    String sing() {
        return verses(1, 12);
    }
}
```
