The header and implementation are consistent with each other. The issue is that the test suite expects the `frequency` function to take only `const std::vector<std::string>& texts` (no `num_threads` parameter). The parallelism should be handled internally based on the number of hardware threads.

Let me update the header to remove the `num_threads` parameter and update the implementation accordingly.

parallel_letter_frequency.h
```cpp
#if !defined(PARALLEL_LETTER_FREQUENCY_H)
#define PARALLEL_LETTER_FREQUENCY_H

#include <map>
#include <string>
#include <vector>

namespace parallel_letter_frequency {

std::map<char, int> frequency(const std::vector<std::string>& texts);

}

#endif
```
