Actually, simpler approach for counting without the borrow issue:

```rust
let mut counts: Vec<(u8, u8)> = Vec::new();
for &r in &ranks {
    let mut found = false;
    for entry in counts.iter_mut() {
        if entry.0 == r {
            entry.1 += 1;
            found = true;
            break;
        }
    }
    if !found {
        counts.push((r, 1));
    }
}
```

This is clean and avoids borrow issues.

