Tokens: 2.3k sent, 430 received.
Applied edit to CircularBuffer.java
response:
The `overwrite` method calls `write`, which declares that it throws `BufferIOException`. Since `overwrite` can never actually throw this exception in a way the caller should detect (when full, it forces the write), I'll add the `throws` clause to `overwrite` to satisfy the compiler.

CircularBuffer.java
```java
class CircularBuffer<T> {

    private final T[] buffer;
    private final int size;
    private int head;
    private int count;

    CircularBuffer(final int size) {
        this.size = size;
        @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
        final T[] tempBuffer = (T[]) new Object[size];
        this.buffer = tempBuffer;
        this.head = 0;
        this.count = 0;
    }

    T read() throws BufferIOException {
        if (count == 0) {
            throw new BufferIOException("Cannot read from an empty buffer.");
        }
        final T data = buffer[head];
        buffer[head] = null;
        head = (head + 1) % size;
        count--;
        return data;
    }

    void write(T data) throws BufferIOException {
        if (count == size) {
            throw new BufferIOException("Cannot write to a full buffer.");
        }
        final int writeIndex = (head + count) % size;
        buffer[writeIndex] = data;
        count++;
    }

    void overwrite(T data) throws BufferIOException {
        if (count == size) {
            buffer[head] = data;
            head = (head + 1) % size;
        } else {
            write(data);
        }
    }

    void clear() {
        for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {
            buffer[i] = null;
        }
        head = 0;
        count = 0;
    }

}
```
