I'll implement the Ten Green Bottles song. The `recite` method needs to return a verse based on the starting number of bottles and how many to take down.

BottleSong.java
```java
class BottleSong {

    String recite(int startBottles, int takeDown) {
        StringBuilder verse = new StringBuilder();
        
        for (int i = 0; i < takeDown; i++) {
            int currentBottles = startBottles - i;
            int nextBottles = currentBottles - 1;
            
            if (i > 0) {
                verse.append("\n");
            }
            
            verse.append(capitalize(numberToWords(currentBottles)));
            verse.append(" green bottle");
            if (currentBottles > 1) {
                verse.append("s");
            }
            verse.append(" hanging on the wall,\n");
            
            verse.append(capitalize(numberToWords(currentBottles)));
            verse.append(" green bottle");
            if (currentBottles > 1) {
                verse.append("s");
            }
            verse.append(" hanging on the wall,\n");
            
            verse.append("And if one green bottle should accidentally fall,\n");
            
            verse.append("There'll be ");
            if (nextBottles == 0) {
                verse.append("no green bottles");
            } else {
                verse.append(numberToWords(nextBottles));
                verse.append(" green bottle");
                if (nextBottles > 1) {
                    verse.append("s");
                }
            }
            verse.append(" hanging on the wall.");
            
            if (i < takeDown - 1) {
                verse.append("\n\n");
            }
        }
        
        return verse.toString();
    }
    
    private String numberToWords(int number) {
        switch (number) {
            case 0: return "no";
            case 1: return "one";
            case 2: return "two";
            case 3: return "three";
            case 4: return "four";
            case 5: return "five";
            case 6: return "six";
            case 7: return "seven";
            case 8: return "eight";
            case 9: return "nine";
            case 10: return "ten";
            default: throw new IllegalArgumentException("Unsupported number: " + number);
        }
    }
    
    private String capitalize(String text) {
        if (text == null || text.isEmpty()) {
            return text;
        }
        return text.charAt(0) + text.substring(1);
    }
}
```
