StateOfTicTacToe.java
```java
class StateOfTicTacToe {
    public GameState determineState(String[] board) {
        int xCount = 0;
        int oCount = 0;
        for (String row : board) {
            for (char c : row.toCharArray()) {
                if (c == 'X') {
                    xCount++;
                } else if (c == 'O') {
                    oCount++;
                }
            }
        }

        // Validate turn order
        if (oCount > xCount || xCount - oCount > 1) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid board: wrong turn order");
        }

        boolean xWins = hasWon(board, 'X');
        boolean oWins = hasWon(board, 'O');

        // Validate win conditions
        if (xWins && oWins) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid board: both players can't win");
        }
        if (xWins && oCount >= xCount) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid board: O won but X has equal or more moves");
        }
        if (oWins && xCount > oCount) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid board: X won but O has fewer moves");
        }

        // Determine game state
        if (xWins || oWins) {
            return GameState.WIN;
        }

        boolean isFull = xCount + oCount == 9;
        if (isFull) {
            return GameState.DRAW;
        }

        return GameState.ONGOING;
    }

    private boolean hasWon(String[] board, char player) {
        // Check rows
        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
            if (board[i].charAt(0) == player && board[i].charAt(1) == player && board[i].charAt(2) == player) {
                return true;
            }
        }
        // Check columns
        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
            if (board[0].charAt(i) == player && board[1].charAt(i) == player && board[2].charAt(i) == player) {
                return true;
            }
        }
        // Check diagonals
        if (board[0].charAt(0) == player && board[1].charAt(1) == player && board[2].charAt(2) == player) {
            return true;
        }
        if (board[0].charAt(2) == player && board[1].charAt(1) == player && board[2].charAt(0) == player) {
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
}
```

I've implemented the state determination logic:

1. **Count marks** - Count X's and O's to validate turn order
2. **Validate turn order** - Since X starts, O can never have more moves than X, and X can have at most one more move than O
3. **Check win conditions** - Both players can't win, and the win must be consistent with the move counts
4. **Determine state**:
   - If someone won → WIN
   - If board is full with no winner → DRAW
   - Otherwise → ONGOING

The `hasWon` method checks all rows, columns, and diagonals for a winning line.
